<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate model accuracy on the LongBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2024</a>)</cite> datasets under varying token budgets for attention computation, the results are shown in Table <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ A.1. Model Accuracy ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ SparseServe: Unlocking Parallelism for Dynamic Sparse Attention in Long-Context LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. The experiments are conducted using the state-of-the-art DSA ArkVale <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>. We observe that both LWM-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu
et al., 2024c</a>)</cite> and Llama3-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pekelis
et al., 2024</a>)</cite> retain <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="99\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>99</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">99\%</annotation></semantics></math> of the accuracy achieved with full attention across all datasets when the token budget is set to 2048. Based on this observation, we adopt a token budget of 2048 for sparse attention in our paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
